		<!-- SettingsEditorNew -->
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_FileDirOperationFailed" type="String">
			<Value>The operation failed. This might be caused from the fact that the path string can be invalid.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_PathCannotBeEmpty" type="String">
			<Value>A file or directory path cannot be empty.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_DownloadedPLTracksDirSelection_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Defines the directory under all the downloaded tracks are saved to.
You can change this directory to your own liking.
Note that if you change the directory, all the currently 
downloaded tracks will be moved there.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ExportedPLTracksDirSelection_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Defines the directory under all the playlist
tracks are exported to.
This is used so that the exported physical 
playlists can find the exported tracks.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ExpBackColorSelection_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Exploration Panel background color.
Modifies the background color of the exploration view to any color 
of your choice.
By default it is set to the system's black color (or any closest to it).
NOTE: The color except from the exploration panel is also used 
in a couple other places. 
See the full documentation for more information.
To modify the color , click on the box inside the border.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ExpForeColorSelection_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Exploration Panel foreground color.
Modifies the foreground color of the exploration view to any color 
of your choice.
By default it is set to the system's white color (or any closest to it).
NOTE: The color except from the exploration panel is also used 
in a couple other places. 
See the full documentation for more information.
To modify the color , click on the box inside the border.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ControllerTrigPrecision_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Controller trigger accuracy.
With this setting, you can properly modify the 
triggers responsiveness behavior.
This allows you to fine-tune the currently attached controller to have the best
responsiveness but also not fire too early when you use them.
Note that the Music Player does not currently define a mapping for these
(are detached at app code level), but if such scenario happens, this is here.
The value set is a ignore range that ignores all 
trigger events below the defined level.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ControllerThumbPrecision_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Controller thumbstick accuracy.
With this setting, you can properly modify the thumbstick 
responsiveness behavior.
This allows you to fine-tune the currently attached controller to have the best
responsiveness but also not fire too early when you use them.
The value set is a ignore range that ignores all 
thumbstick events below the defined level.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ControllerTimeoutDelay_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Controller Thread Timeout Delay.
This value should only be modified on advanced scenarios, 
because this modifies when the controller thread will capture a new 
controller state snapshot. Move it to larger values in case of driver
discrepancies and/or increased input responsiveness latency.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_AudioDeviceLatency_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Audio device buffering latency.
Modifies the time between two new I/O requests while doing playback.
Lower values achieve better precision on the reported time,
while larger ones allow less I/O requests to be performed.
However, when you find yourself in a case where the track
'skips' samples (parts) of it, you should increase this value.
This is especially true for slow computers and/or drives.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_AudioDeviceSelection_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Audio device selection.
Have you changed your mind on which audio device all the
tracks are playing? You can change the playback target 
from this box here.
After pressing the 'Confirm...' button the settings editor will
close in order to modify the setting, because it must
directly modify a critical state inside the Music Player.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_TitleText" type="String">
			<Value>Music Player Settings - Version {0}</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_RootText" type="String">
			<Value>Settings Root Object</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_BrokenDescTextWarn" type="String">
			<Value>Cannot load a description string.
You should add a description string 
for the item {0}</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_BrokenDescTextWarn_ResNotFound" type="String">
			<Value>The resource loader cannot find the resource 
named as {0}.
The resource will not be loaded.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_CannotLoadSettingsObject" type="String">
			<Value>Cannot apply the settings object due to an underlying exception:
{0}</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_WelcomeAndUsageMessage" type="String">
			<Value>Welcome to the new and revamped Music Player Settings!
From the tree in the left , you can open it's nodes to find the currently 
defined settings that are defined for the app.
Then, you modify the setting as you expect.
Note that you must apply the new setting value
by pressing the 'Confirm...' button. If you do not do that,
the setting will keep it's last value, whatever that was.
See the below image to take an idea of how it looks like...</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_SettingNotSelected" type="String">
			<Value>A setting has not been selected! Select a setting now.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_ValidValueFromValuesNotSelected" type="String">
			<Value>An item was not selected yet! Select an item first.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_ApplyNewDeviceNow" type="String">
			<Value>Apply the new device to the Music Player now?
Press 'Yes' to confirm, or use 'No' to skip doing this.
Note that the settings editor will close if you confirm this action.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_CannotFindYtDlpInstallationFile" type="String">
			<Value>The app cannot find the YtDlp installation verification data.
The installation is potentially broken.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingsEditorNew_VerifyYtDlpInstallationDataQuestion" type="String">
			<Value>Are you sure that you want to verify the YtDlp installation?
Use 'Yes' to proceed , or use 'No' to cancel.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_TrackName_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the Track Name column width when in Playlist mode.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_TrackCreationTime_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the Track Creation Time column
width when in Playlist mode.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_TrackSize_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the Track Size column width when in Playlist mode.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_TrackContribArtists_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the Track Contributing 
Artists column width when in Playlist mode.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_TrackNumber_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the Track Number column width when in Playlist mode.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_EncodedBy_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the Encoded By column width when in Playlist mode.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_Album_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the Album column width when in Playlist mode.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_PlaylistName_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the Playlist Name column width 
when selecting/picking a playlist.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_CreationTime_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the File Creation Time 
column width when selecting/picking a playlist.
			</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_LastPlaylistTrack_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the Last Playlist Track 
column width when selecting/picking a playlist.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="SettingTree_ColWidth_FileName_Desc" type="String">
			<Value>Modifies the File Name column width when 
searching for files to add to a new playlist.</Value>
		</Data>
		<!-- CreditsPane -->
		<Data name="CreditsPane_HeaderText" type="String">
			<Value>The Music Player On .NET 8 is an application that requires support libraries in order to work.
This window lists those external libraries and it's respective authors.
Along with these, there is also here my license for my own code.</Value>
		</Data>
		<!-- PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm -->
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_UsageDesc" type="String">
			<Value>Playlist Archive Options. Through this dialog you can define more archived playlist
attributes to be saved so as to present these to the consumers of this playlist.
You can use one of the default attributes that are defined , or you may also define your own ones.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_IsCustomAttrDesc" type="String">
			<Value>This attribute is a custom one and does not have a description.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_ProvideAttributeNameText" type="String">
			<Value>Provide the name of the custom attribute on the below text box.
Confirm the new attribute name by pressing the 'Add...' button below.
If you want to cancel the operation, delete the text and press the 'Add...' button.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_DefinedAsReadOnlyAttribute" type="String">
			<Value>The attribute attempted to be added is existing and is readonly.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_AttributeNotSelected" type="String">
			<Value>An attribute was not selected so as to update it's value.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_SpecifyReadOnlyAttrText" type="String">
			<Value>Register this attribute as an readonly-attribute...</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_ATTR_Creator" type="String">
			<Value>Defines the creator of this playlist.
By default it is set to the name of the current Windows User.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_ATTR_CreationTime" type="String">
			<Value>Specifies a timestamp of the creation date and time of this archived playlist.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_ATTR_Comment" type="String">
			<Value>Specifies an optional comment for the playlist.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_ATTR_Name" type="String">
			<Value>Specifies a custom internal name for the playlist.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="PlaylistArchiveOptionsForm_ATTR_CompressionMethod" type="String">
			<Value>Specifies the compression method to use for the new archive. It's current values are:
-> Store, which does just plainly store the playlist files,
-> GZip, stores the files using the GZip algorithm,
-> BZip2, stores the files using the BZip2 algorithm.</Value>
		</Data>
		<!-- ArchivedPlaylistInformationForm -->
		<Data name="ArchivedPlaylistInformationForm_NoAttributesFound" type="String">
			<Value>This playlist was written with an older version of the Music Player
that does not support custom attributes and information.
Press 'OK' to return back.</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="ArchivedPlaylistInformationForm_PrimaryData" type="String">
			<Value>Playlist Name: {0}
Playlist Creator: {1}
Playlist Creation Date: {2}</Value>
		</Data>
		<Data name="ArchivedPlaylistInformationForm_AdditionalInfoLabelText" type="String">
			<Value>Additional discovered attributes &amp;&amp; preferences:</Value>
		</Data>
	</ResData>
